1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
Sun Wukong rose from a stone egg

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:05,040
and became king of the monkeys.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,040
But victories on earth were not enough;

4
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:11,060
he wanted recognition from Heaven itself.

5
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,300
The celestial court gave him a minor

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,020
post, thinking it would contain him.

7
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,180
When he learned how little the title

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,640
meant, the Monkey King rebelled.

9
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,640
He stole celestial peaches,

10
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:26,300
disrupted a banquet,

11
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:29,220
and survived attempts to destroy him.

12
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,320
Even heavenly troops struggled to bring him

13
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:32,855
to heel.

14
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,400
At last the Buddha challenged him to

15
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,460
escape the palm of his hand.

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,840
Wukong leapt to what he thought was

17
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,200
the end of the universe.

18
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,820
The pillars he marked were only fingers.

19
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,300
His limitless journey had never left the

20
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,320
Buddha’s palm. A mountain then held him

21
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:52,880
fast.

22
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,480
His story did not end in defeat.

23
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,420
Later, the same unruly strength would be

24
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:02,000
redirected into a pilgrimage,

25
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:04,920
where power had to learn restraint.
